# Part 11's control arm RUNS this program (panel 226's R1, 2026-10-20): the
# strict build refuses it under `non_exhaustive`, a thesis rule, and the control arm,
# `build --permissive`, gives the dropped rule the meaning the sitting's
# table pins: a `match` missing a case prints the arms it takes and aborts at the case no arm names, `panic: this match has no arm for .dot`, never *this is a compiler bug*.
# The witness is the compiler-engineer's (w01-non_exhaustive), one of 27 it ran before the
# resolution was written (`docs/panel/226-reports/compiler-engineer.md`).

variant Shape
    circle
        r: i64
    square
        s: i64
    dot

function area(sh: Shape) -> i64
    return match sh  #~ non_exhaustive
        .circle c => c.r * c.r * 3
        .square q => q.s * q.s

function main()
    print(area(.square(s: 2)))
    print(area(.dot))
